      "text": "5,178,526,  874.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nHmm, I think I made a mistake in adding the numbers. Let me recalculate the sum:\n\n576,774 (from the ones place) plus 1,281,720 (from the tens place) equals 1,858,494.\n\nAdding 32,043,000 (from the hundreds place) brings the total to 33,901,494.\n\nAdding 0 (from the thousands place) doesn't change the total.\n\nFinally, adding 5,126,880,000 (from the ten-thousands place) results in 5,160,781,494.\n\nSo, the correct product of 64,086 and 80,529 is 5,160,781,494.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 64086 and 80529?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of **64,086** and **80,529** step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 64,086 by 9 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   64,086 \\times 9 = 576,774\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 64,086 by 20 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   64,086 \\times 20 = 1,281,720\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 64,086 by 500 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   64,086 \\times 500 = 32,043,000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 64,086 by 0 (thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   64,086 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 64,086 by 80,000 (ten-thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   64,086 \\times 80,000 = 5,126,880,000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n576,774 + 1,281,720 + 32,043,000 + 0 + 5,126,880,000 = 5,160,781,494\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{5,\\!160,\\!781,\\!494}\\).",
