      "text": "2,819,  138,  29,028 multiplied by 97,138 equals 2,819,  138.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nStarting over, I'll multiply 29,028 by 97,138 step by step:\n\n1. 29,028 \u00d7 8 = 232,224\n2. 29,028 \u00d7 30 = 870,840\n3. 29,028 \u00d7 100 = 2,902,800\n4. 29,028 \u00d7 7,000 = 203,196,000\n5. 29,028 \u00d7 90,000 = 2,612,520,000\n\nNow, adding all these together:\n\n232,224 + 870,840 = 1,103,064\n\n1,103,064 + 2,902,800 = 4,005,864\n\n4,005,864 + 203,196,000 = 207,201,864\n\n207,201,864 + 2,612,520,000 = 2,819,721,864\n\nSo, the correct product of 29,028 and 97,138 is 2,819,721,864.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 29028 and 97138?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nTo find the product of **29,028** and **97,138**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step based on the place value of each digit in **97,138**.\n\n1. **Multiply 29,028 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   29,028 \\times 8 = 232,224\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 29,028 by the tens place digit (30):**\n   \\[\n   29,028 \\times 30 = 870,840\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 29,028 by the hundreds place digit (100):**\n   \\[\n   29,028 \\times 100 = 2,902,800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 29,028 by the thousands place digit (7,000):**\n   \\[\n   29,028 \\times 7,000 = 203,196,000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 29,028 by the ten-thousands place digit (90,000):**\n   \\[\n   29,028 \\times 90,000 = 2,612,520,000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n232,224 + 870,840 + 2,902,800 + 203,196,000 + 2,612,520,000 = 2,819,721,864\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{2,\\!819,\\!721,\\!864}\\).",
