      "text": "2,229,040,  1234.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nHmm, I think I made a mistake in adding the partial products. Let me recalculate the sum carefully.\n\nAdding 590,412 + 2,952,060 + 59,041,200 + 196,804,000 + 1,968,040,000 gives me a total of 2,227,427,672.\n\nThat seems more accurate. I must have added incorrectly the first time.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 98402 and 22636?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of **98,402** and **22,636** step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 98,402 by 6 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!402 \\times 6 = 590,\\!412\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 98,402 by 30 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!402 \\times 30 = 2,\\!952,\\!060\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 98,402 by 600 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!402 \\times 600 = 59,\\!041,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 98,402 by 2,000 (thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!402 \\times 2,\\!000 = 196,\\!804,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 98,402 by 20,000 (ten-thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!402 \\times 20,\\!000 = 1,\\!968,\\!040,\\!000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n590,\\!412 + 2,\\!952,\\!060 + 59,\\!041,\\!200 + 196,\\!804,\\!000 + 1,\\!968,\\!040,\\!000 = 2,\\!227,\\!427,\\!672\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{2,\\!227,\\!427,\\!672}\\).",
