      "text": "7,932,127,  134.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nHmm, I think I made a mistake in adding the partial products. Let me recalculate the sum carefully.\n\nAdding 182,954, 0, 54,886,200, 548,862,000, and 7,318,160,000 together gives me a total of 7,916,911,154.\n\nThat seems more accurate. I must have added incorrectly the first time. It's important to carefully add each partial product to ensure the final result is correct.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 91477 and 86602?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of **91,477** and **86,602** step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 91,477 by 2 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   91,\\!477 \\times 2 = 182,\\!954\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 91,477 by 0 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   91,\\!477 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 91,477 by 600 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   91,\\!477 \\times 600 = 54,\\!886,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 91,477 by 6,000 (thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   91,\\!477 \\times 6,\\!000 = 548,\\!862,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 91,477 by 80,000 (ten-thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   91,\\!477 \\times 80,\\!000 = 7,\\!318,\\!160,\\!000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n182,\\!954 + 0 + 54,\\!886,\\!200 + 548,\\!862,\\!000 + 7,\\!318,\\!160,\\!000 = 7,\\!916,\\!911,\\!154\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{7,\\!916,\\!911,\\!154}\\).",
