messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 20665 and 46803?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 20665 and 46803. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable steps.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 20665 by each digit of 46803, taking into account the place value of each digit. This means I'll multiply 20665 by 3 (the ones place), then by 0 (the tens place), followed by 800 (the hundreds place), then by 6000 (the thousands place), and finally by 40000 (the ten-thousands place).\n\nAfter obtaining each of these partial products, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures that I handle each part of the multiplication accurately and systematically.\n. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
