messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 19186 and 45008?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n.\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 19,186 and 45,008. To make this easier, I'll break down 45,008 into its place values: 40,000, 5,000, 80, and 8.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 19,186 by each of these components separately.\n\n1. Multiplying 19,186 by 40,000:.\n   19,186 × 40,000 = 767,440,000.\n\n2. Multiplying 19,186 by 5,000:.\n   19,186 × 5,000 = 95,930,000.\n\n3. Multiplying 19,186 by 80:.\n   19,186 × 80 = 1,534,880.\n\n4. Multiplying 19,186 by 8:.\n   19,186 × 8 = 153,488.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these results together to find the total product:. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
