messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 21697 and 40609?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n.\nFirst, I need to multiply 21697 by 40609. To make this easier, I'll break down 40609 into its place values: 40000, 600, and 9.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 21697 by each of these components separately.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 21697 by 9:.\n21697 × 9 = 195,273.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 21697 by 600:.\n21697 × 600 = 13,018,200.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 21697 by 40,000:.\n21697 × 40,000 = 867,880,000.\n\nAfter obtaining these partial products, I'll add them all together to get the final result:. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
