      "index": 0,
      "text": "2,385,  160.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 27,740 by 6 (the ones place of 86,016), which gives me 166,440.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 27,740 by 10 (the tens place), resulting in 277,400.\n\nThen, multiplying by 0 (the hundreds place) gives 0.\n\nMultiplying by 6 (the thousands place) yields 166,440,000.\n\nFinally, multiplying by 8 (the ten-thousands place) results in 221,920,000.\n\nAdding all these partial products together: 166,440 + 277,400 + 0 + 166,440,000 + 221,920,000 equals 389,803,840.\n\nSo, the correct product of 27,740 and 86,016 is 389,803,840.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 27740 and 86016?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nTo find the product of **27,740** and **86,016**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 27,740 by 6 (ones place of 86,016):**\n   \\[\n   27,\\!740 \\times 6 = 166,\\!440\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 27,740 by 10 (tens place of 86,016):**\n   \\[\n   27,\\!740 \\times 10 = 277,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 27,740 by 0 (hundreds place of 86,016):**\n   \\[\n   27,\\!740 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 27,740 by 600 (thousands place of 86,016):**\n   \\[\n   27,\\!740 \\times 600 = 16,\\!644,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 27,740 by 80,000 (ten-thousands place of 86,016):**\n   \\[\n   27,\\!740 \\times 80,\\!000 = 2,\\!219,\\!200,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n6. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   166,\\!440 + 277,\\!400 + 0 + 16,\\!644,\\!000 + 2,\\!219,\\!200,\\!000 = 389,\\!803,\\!840\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of **27,740** and **86,016** is \\(\\boxed{389,\\!803,\\!840}\\).",
