      "text": "265,172,290.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 10110 and 26239?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of **10110** and **26239** step by step.\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   We'll break down **26239** into its place values:\n   \\[\n   26239 = 20000 + 6000 + 200 + 30 + 9\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply each part by 10110:**\n   \n   - **Multiply by 20000:**\n     \\[\n     10110 \\times 20000 = 202,\\!200,\\!000\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Multiply by 6000:**\n     \\[\n     10110 \\times 6000 = 60,\\!660,\\!000\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Multiply by 200:**\n     \\[\n     10110 \\times 200 = 2,\\!022,\\!000\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Multiply by 30:**\n     \\[\n     10110 \\times 30 = 303,\\!300\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Multiply by 9:**\n     \\[\n     10110 \\times 9 = 90,\\!990\n     \\]\n\n3. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   202,\\!200,\\!000 + 60,\\!660,\\!000 + 2,\\!022,\\!000 + 303,\\!300 + 90,\\!990 = 265,\\!172,\\!290\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\n\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{265,\\!172,\\!290}\\).",
